    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **46 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp33Tests.errorRejectsFutureDate`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `POST /api/owners` pipeline now rejects a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date with a 400, following the existing OfficeFloor function-injection conventions in this repo:\n\n1. **`RejectFutureRegistrationDate`** (new function) \u2014 reads the validated body (`@Val OwnerFieldsDto`) and throws a checked `FutureRegistrationDateException` when `registrationDate` is present and `isAfter(LocalDate.now())`. An absent date (which defaults to the server date downstream) or a date on/before today passes untouched.\n\n2. **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** (new checked exception, `extends Exception`) so it surfaces in the `throws` clause and routes to an escalation handler.\n\n3. **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `400` with `{\"errors\": [\"registrationDate\"]}`, mirroring the existing `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler`.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/\u2026FutureRegistrationDateException.yml` wiring the exception to the handler.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `rejectFutureRegistrationDate` step after `validatePostcode` and before `ensureCityCapacity`/`resolveRegistrationDate`, so a future date is rejected early, before any transactional/business-day work runs.\n\nThe check is placed *before* `ResolveRegistrationDate` (the business-day roll), so the raw supplied date is validated rather than a rolled-forward one, and existing behavior (weekend roll, default date, membership numbering) is unaffected \u2014 confirmed by `Cp07/Cp14/Cp20/Cp21` still passing.",
